.TH CPPKG-CLI 1 "2026-05-19" "cppkg-cli 1.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cppkg-cli \- Download C/C++ packages into a shared include directory or project workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cppkg-cli
[cppkg\-cli [options] [command]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download C/C++ packages into a shared include directory or project workspace
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output the version number
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error output
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli add
Add one dependency to cppkg.json, optionally installing it
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I source
Required. GitHub owner/repo, GitHub/Gitee repository URL, or direct zip archive URL
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-name <name>
Dependency name to write in cppkg.json
.TP
.B \-\-tag <tag>
Install a specific release tag or repository tag
.TP
.B \-\-branch <branch>
Install a specific repository branch
.TP
.B \-\-version\-range <range>
Install the latest release matching a semantic version range
.TP
.B \-\-version\-policy <policy>
Manifest version policy: latest\-release, latest\-prerelease, or default\-branch
.TP
.B \-\-prerelease
Allow prerelease versions when selecting the latest release
.TP
.B \-\-full\-project
Install the package as a full project and skip include\-directory detection
.TP
.B \-\-include\-path <path>
Archive\-relative include directory to write in cppkg.json; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-prefix <path>
Archive\-relative directory to install from
.TP
.B \-\-patches <path>
Project\-relative patch file to apply after extraction; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-components <name>
Top\-level include/project entry to install; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-checksum <sha256>
Expected archive SHA\-256 checksum
.TP
.B \-\-install
Install the dependency after writing cppkg.json
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Replace an existing manifest dependency
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass cached archives when used with \-\-install
.TP
.B \-\-http\-proxy <url>
HTTP request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-https\-proxy <url>
HTTPS request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Log what would be added without writing to manifest
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Only use cached archives, no network requests
.TP
.B \-\-no\-transitive
Skip resolution of transitive dependencies when installing
.TP
.B \-\-workspace <package\-name>
Add dependency to a specific workspace member, or use \[cq]all\[cq] for all members
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli add nlohmann/json
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli add fmtlib/fmt \-\-name fmt \-\-tag 11.2.0 \-\-install
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli add nlohmann/json \-\-dry\-run
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli audit
Check installed packages against known vulnerabilities
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-level <severity>
Filter advisories by minimum severity (low, medium, high, critical)
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Suggest updates for packages with vulnerabilities
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output results as JSON
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli audit
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli audit \-\-level high \-\-fix
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli get
Download GitHub repositories or remote zip archives into the configured package directory
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I repo\-urls
Required. One or more GitHub repository URLs, GitHub API repository URLs, Gitee repository URLs, or direct zip archive URLs separated by spaces
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-full\-project
Install the package as a full project and skip include\-directory detection
.TP
.B \-\-tag <tag>
Install a specific release tag or repository tag
.TP
.B \-\-branch <branch>
Install a specific repository branch
.TP
.B \-\-version\-range <range>
Install the latest release matching a semantic version range
.TP
.B \-\-version\-policy <policy>
Version policy: latest\-release, latest\-prerelease, or default\-branch
.TP
.B \-\-prerelease
Allow prerelease versions when selecting the latest release
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass cached archives and refresh downloads
.TP
.B \-\-include\-path <path>
Archive\-relative include directory to install; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-prefix <path>
Archive\-relative directory to install from
.TP
.B \-\-patches <path>
Project\-relative patch file to apply after extraction; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-components <name>
Top\-level include/project entry to install; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-checksum <sha256>
Expected archive SHA\-256 checksum
.TP
.B \-\-binary [spec]
Install pre\-built binaries (platform/arch format, e.g. linux/x64)
.TP
.B \-\-http\-proxy <url>
HTTP request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-https\-proxy <url>
HTTPS request proxy, overrides config
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli get https://github.com/nlohmann/json
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli get https://github.com/fmtlib/fmt \-\-version\-range \[cq]^11.0.0\[cq]
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli get https://gitlab.com/libname/lib \-\-binary linux/x64
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli import
Import dependencies from vcpkg.json or conanfile.txt into cppkg.json
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I file
Required. Path to vcpkg.json, conanfile.txt, or auto\-detect from filename
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be imported without writing
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Replace existing dependencies instead of merging
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli import vcpkg.json
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli import conanfile.txt \-\-dry\-run
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli import vcpkg.json \-\-replace
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli init
Create a cppkg.json package manifest
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Overwrite an existing cppkg.json
.TP
.B \-\-no\-gitignore
Skip .gitignore creation or modification
.TP
.B \-\-workspace
Create a cppkg\-workspace.json workspace configuration
.TP
.B \-\-template <type>
Scaffold a project template: cmake\-header\-only, cmake\-executable, cmake\-library
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli init
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli init \-\-force
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli init \-\-workspace
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli compile
Compile C/C++ source files with cppkg include paths
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I files
Required. C/C++ source files to compile
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-compiler <command>
Compiler command (default: c++)
.TP
.B \-\-toolchain <name>
Compiler profile from cppkg\-toolchains.json
.TP
.B \-\-std <standard>
C++ language standard
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output <path>
Output binary path
.TP
.B \-I, \-\-include\-dir <path>
Additional include directory; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-compiler\-arg <arg>
Additional compiler or linker argument; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-docker
Run the compiler inside Docker
.TP
.B \-\-docker\-image <image>
Docker image to use with \-\-docker
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the compiler command without executing it
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli compile src/main.cpp \-o app
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli compile src/main.cpp \-\-toolchain gcc\-14 \-\-docker \-\-dry\-run
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli bug
Open the cppkg\-cli issue tracker in the default browser
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli build
Configure and build a CMake project with cppkg include paths
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-build\-dir <path>
CMake build directory
.TP
.B \-\-compiler <command>
C++ compiler command for CMake
.TP
.B \-\-toolchain <name>
Compiler profile from cppkg\-toolchains.json
.TP
.B \-\-std <standard>
C++ language standard
.TP
.B \-\-release
Use Release build configuration
.TP
.B \-\-config <name>
CMake build configuration
.TP
.B \-\-target <target>
CMake target to build
.TP
.B \-\-generator <name>
CMake generator name
.TP
.B \-\-cmake\-arg <arg>
Additional CMake configure argument; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-build\-arg <arg>
Additional CMake build argument; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cppkg\-cmake
Do not generate or inject cppkg.cmake during configure
.TP
.B \-\-docker
Run CMake configure and build inside Docker
.TP
.B \-\-docker\-image <image>
Docker image to use with \-\-docker
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print CMake command(s) without executing them
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli build \-\-release
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli build \-\-toolchain clang\-18 \-\-docker \-\-dry\-run
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli compiler
Manage compiler versions and Docker\-backed compiler profiles
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli compiler list
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli compiler install clang\-18 \-\-set\-default
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli create
Scaffold a new C/C++ library project
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I name
Required. Name of the new project
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-header\-only
Create a header\-only library (skip src/ and CMake)
.TP
.B \-\-c
Create a C project instead of C++
.TP
.B \-\-output <dir>
Custom output directory
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli create my\-lib
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli create my\-lib \-\-header\-only \-\-c \-\-output ./libs/my\-lib
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli install
Install dependencies declared in cppkg.json
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I packages
Optional dependency names, repository paths, package names, or source URLs from cppkg.json
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-http\-proxy <url>
HTTP request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-https\-proxy <url>
HTTPS request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass cached archives and refresh downloads
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Only use cached archives, no network requests
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Log what would be installed without downloading
.TP
.B \-\-frozen\-lockfile
Require cppkg\-lock.json to match cppkg.json before installing
.TP
.B \-\-no\-transitive
Skip resolution of transitive dependencies
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli install
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli install json fmt \-\-frozen\-lockfile
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli install \-\-workspace \-\-no\-transitive
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli integrate
Modify CMakeLists.txt to auto\-include cppkg headers and projects
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be changed without writing
.TP
.B \-\-target <name>
Integrate only for a specific CMake target
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli integrate
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli integrate \-\-dry\-run
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli integrate \-\-target my\-app
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli inspect
Inspect C/C++ source includes and report package needs
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-add
Add recommended missing package candidates to cppkg.json
.TP
.B \-\-install
Add and install recommended missing package candidates
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Replace existing manifest dependencies when adding
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass cached archives when used with \-\-install
.TP
.B \-\-http\-proxy <url>
HTTP request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-https\-proxy <url>
HTTPS request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output result as JSON
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli inspect
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli inspect \-\-add \-\-install
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli list
List installed packages tracked in the configured deps file
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-tree
Show a tree view of installed dependencies
.TP
.B \-\-graph
Alias for \-\-tree
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as JSON
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli list
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli list \-\-tree
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli lockfile
Manage cppkg\-lock.json
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli pack
Create a distributable tarball of the current project
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-output <path>
Output file path
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli publish
Publish the project as a package archive to GitHub releases
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-registry <url>
GitHub API base URL for publishing
.TP
.B \-\-tag <tag>
Release tag (defaults to latest git tag or v0.0.0)
.TP
.B \-\-name <name>
Release name (defaults to the release tag)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Preview what would be published without actually publishing
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli publish
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli publish \-\-tag v2.0.0 \-\-name \[cq]Version 2.0\[cq]
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli rebuild
Reinstall all packages from scratch (clean + install)
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli remove
Remove an installed package from the configured install directory
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I package
Required. Installed package name, repository path, owner/repo, or GitHub/Gitee repository URL
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Log what would be removed without deleting
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli remove json
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli remove json \-\-dry\-run
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli search
Search GitHub for C/C++ libraries sorted by stars
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I query
Required. Search terms, for example json parser
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-limit <number>
Maximum number of results to show, capped at 50
.TP
.B \-\-language <language>
GitHub language qualifier
.TP
.B \-\-install
Install after selecting a result; kept for compatibility because search is interactive by default
.TP
.B \-\-no\-interactive
Only print results without opening the selector
.TP
.B \-\-select <number>
Non\-interactive selection index to install
.TP
.B \-\-full\-project
Install the selected package as a full project and skip include\-directory detection
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass cached archives and refresh downloads
.TP
.B \-\-http\-proxy <url>
HTTP request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-https\-proxy <url>
HTTPS request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output search results as JSON
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli search json
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli search http client \-\-limit 20
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli server
Start a local web server for browsing and downloading packages
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-host <host>
Host interface to bind the server to
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-port <port>
Port to listen on; use 0 to choose a random open port
.TP
.B \-\-http\-proxy <url>
HTTP request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-https\-proxy <url>
HTTPS request proxy, overrides config
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli server
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli server \-\-host 0.0.0.0 \-\-port 4936
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli status
Check cppkg manifest, lockfile, metadata, and installed files
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as JSON
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli status
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli update
Update one installed package, or all tracked packages when no selector is provided
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I package
Installed package name, repository path, owner/repo, or GitHub/Gitee repository URL
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-full\-project
Force full\-project reinstall; without this flag the recorded install mode is reused
.TP
.B \-\-tag <tag>
Update one package from a specific release tag or repository tag
.TP
.B \-\-branch <branch>
Update one package from a specific branch
.TP
.B \-\-version\-range <range>
Update one package to the latest release matching a semantic version range
.TP
.B \-\-version\-policy <policy>
Update one package with a version policy: latest\-release, latest\-prerelease, or default\-branch
.TP
.B \-\-prerelease
Allow prerelease versions when selecting the latest release
.TP
.B \-\-include\-path <path>
Archive\-relative include directory to install; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-prefix <path>
Archive\-relative directory to install from
.TP
.B \-\-patches <path>
Project\-relative patch file to apply after extraction; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-components <name>
Top\-level include/project entry to install; may be repeated
.TP
.B \-\-checksum <sha256>
Expected archive SHA\-256 checksum
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Bypass cached archives and refresh downloads
.TP
.B \-\-http\-proxy <url>
HTTP request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-https\-proxy <url>
HTTPS request proxy, overrides config
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli update
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli update fmt \-\-tag 11.2.0
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli vendor
Copy installed packages from cpp_libs/ into a vendor/ directory
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-originals
Delete the cpp_libs/ directory after vendoring
.TP
.B \-\-output <dir>
Custom output directory (defaults to vendor/)
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli vendor
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli vendor \-\-output ./third_party \-\-remove\-originals
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli cache
Manage downloaded archive cache
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli cache list
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli cache clean \-\-older\-than 30
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli clean
Remove installed packages, cache, and lockfile
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-all
Remove all cppkg data including cpp_libs/ and lockfile
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Skip confirmation prompt
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be removed without deleting
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output result as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli cmake
Generate a cppkg.cmake integration helper
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output <path>
Project\-relative output path
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Overwrite an existing cppkg.cmake
.RE
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli cmake
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli cmake \-\-output cmake/cppkg.cmake \-\-force
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli completion
Generate shell completion scripts
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I shell
Required. Shell type: bash, zsh, fish, or powershell
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli config
Manage project\-level cppkg settings in ./cppkg.config.json
.RS
Examples:
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli config list
.IP
.B cppkg\-cli config set cacheDirName cache
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli diff
Show differences between manifest and lockfile
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output result as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli diagnose
Diagnose the environment for cppkg\-cli
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output result as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli docs
Open the cppkg\-cli documentation site in the default browser
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli home
Open the cppkg\-cli GitHub repository in the default browser
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli env
Show system environment diagnostics
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli exec
Run a command with CPPKG_INCLUDE_DIR and CPPKG_PROJECTS_DIR in environment
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I command
Required. Command and arguments to execute
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli graph
Visualize dependency graph as ASCII tree, DOT, or Mermaid
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-format <format>
Output format: ascii, dot, or mermaid
.TP
.B \-\-depth <number>
Limit dependency graph depth (requires a positive integer)
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output dependency tree as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli info
Show detailed information about an installed package
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I package
Required. Installed package name or selector
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output result as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli licenses
Scan installed packages for open\-source licenses
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-full
Show full license text
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli migrate
Migrate packages to/from vcpkg and Conan formats
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli outdated
Check installed packages for newer available versions
.RS
Arguments:
.TP
.I packages
Optional package names to check; checks all if omitted
.RE
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-http\-proxy <url>
HTTP request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-https\-proxy <url>
HTTPS request proxy, overrides config
.TP
.B \-\-prerelease
Include prerelease versions when checking
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B cppkg\-cli self\-update
Check for a newer version of cppkg\-cli
.RS
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-install
Automatically install the latest version
